{
  "name": "vault_market",
  "description": "Non-derivable-genesis fixture IDL. Anchor-shaped: `type`-wrapped account layouts carry 8-byte discriminators the program writes itself, one instruction account is program-constrained (`pda`), one is an SPL token account the adapter decodes, one is pinned to a literal oracle address, and one is not declared by the adapter at all. No binary is needed: the classifier reads the IDL, it does not run the program.",
